WEBVTT

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.520
There.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.310
Thanks.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:25.810
It's nothing.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.650
Is everyone else okay?

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.610
You look tired.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:39.330
Is there a reason you're not singing
the Song of Healing?

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.410
Finis!

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.080
Henry!

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.880
You--? You came back all this way?

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:54.920
You look exhausted.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:57.720
I used the power of songs too much.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:02.560
If I sing just one more song,
I'm sure I'd--

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.230
You don't have to sing again.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:05.930
THE SONG OF GOODBYE

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.640
Wasn't that amazing? We were flying!

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.520
I didn't think we could really fly either!

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.400
The value of the wind power
with respect to the overall mass

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.230
was scientifically a little--

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:18.940
I got it, I got it!

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:21.360
Do you think he's okay?

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.990
-That hot blond guy.
-You're too young to talk like that.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.870
You're right.
I'm worried about Mr. Leobolt.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:31.620
He's strong, I'm sure he got away.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.130
But if they lay one finger on him,

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:36.210
I'm going to crush
those Capital Army guys!

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:37.670
I think she's serious.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:43.720
<i>I'm sure there are people who are waiting</i>
<i>to hear your songs, Rin.</i>

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:49.180
What if the person who's waiting
to hear my songs is--?

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.940
<i>Mr. Leobolt mentioned</i>
<i>that there's another woman</i>

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.110
<i>who has the power of songs.</i>

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:58.690
Miss Finis!

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.280
Corte!

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.030
I'm so glad you're okay!

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:08.200
Mr. Leobolt, we don't have much time left.
Prince Rudo is nearby.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.250
And he knows about you two.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.120
Oh, there you are, Finis!

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.800
This is the frontline region.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.760
Why did you come
to a dangerous place like this?

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:28.850
It doesn't matter.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.770
The Court Orchestra is about to arrive
from the Capital.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.190
The Court Orchestra?

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.190
The power of songs becomes stronger

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:40.820
when there's music and rhythm,
much more powerful than singing alone.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:45.660
You have to use your overwhelming power
to quickly capture the enemy fortress.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.870
Or else someone is going to get killed.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:50.740
It can't be...

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.370
So, that's what was happening.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.960
In order to protect me,

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.800
she used the power of songs to attack...

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:03.090
Wait!

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:07.470
When Miss Finis uses the power of songs,
her life becomes shorter!

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:08.970
So, please!

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.140
Who are you?

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:15.730
What do you think you're doing,
butting in?

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.150
Prince Rudo!

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:26.820
Corte!

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.990
We don't need the power of songs.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:32.490
We'll capture Mont Valay fortress
on our own.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.410
That would take too long.
I reject your plan.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:39.130
What if I told you we could finish
before the Court Orchestra arrives?

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:40.790
What did you say?

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.090
You want to help Finis?

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:48.840
She might be waiting for my songs.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:50.390
Rin...

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:52.510
You guys all said it, right?

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.850
That my songs have the power
to cheer people up.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:57.140
That's why...

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:00.310
even if I was able to sing in the Capital,

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.110
I wouldn't want to!

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:06.070
I can't just ignore people
who I might be able to help!

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:12.450
That's why I have to sing for Finis!

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.060
Cute!

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:41.690
Hey, Allu. Can I make him jump
through a ring of fire?

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.980
No. That's someone else's dog.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:47.570
So, this is the home
of the famous Dr. Weissen.

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:50.200
Hey, what are we going to do next?

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:54.280
He might be able
to tell us something about Finis.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:59.910
And that hottie looked into my eyes
while he said so, right?

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.250
He said, "Go to Dr. Weissen's laboratory,
it's safe there,

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:06.090
-and let's get married."
-He didn't say that.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.470
Who is this doctor guy, anyway?

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:11.090
You don't know?

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.760
Dr. Weissen is a genius inventor

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:16.970
who designed the airship,
an archaeologist,

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.600
and a great scientist

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:22.100
admired throughout the entire world!

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.780
What do you women and children want?

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.950
Are you the famous--?

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:48.960
I don't like trouble. Go home.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:51.380
What? We haven't
even said anything yet...

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:52.720
Welcome! Welcome!

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.140
-Go home.
-Welcome!

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.140
Which one is it?

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:00.600
-Go home.
-Welcome!

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:03.390
Which one is it?

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:06.400
-Welcome!
-Welcome.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.160
This is the blueprint for the airship!

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.660
It's drawn in such great detail!

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:20.910
Don't touch it!

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:22.790
Sorry!

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:27.170
This is a diagram of the power path.
The power source is on this one.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.050
I have more related to the design
on the second floor.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.340
If you want to see them, let me know.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:35.220
Ah, thank you.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:38.890
Honestly. Kids these days...
They don't know restraint.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.890
You must be tired from traveling.

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:45.480
I made some tea, so drink up.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:48.230
Tea? Isn't this wine?

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:50.730
It's the blood
of a giant venomous snake.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:52.030
It's not even wine!

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.490
-Drink up.
-How am I supposed to drink this?!

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:57.740
What? I thought you would test
whether it has any poison for me.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:04.660
She drank everything!

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:07.040
-Hold on. Are you okay?
-That was disgusting!

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.420
But I was thirsty.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.380
You're an honest girl.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:14.510
Good.

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:16.800
It looks like this one is drinkable.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.850
What's wrong with this old man?

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:23.020
So...

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:25.430
what brings you here?

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.270
Well, we're looking
for someone named Finis.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:30.690
Do you know her?

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:33.900
I don't know her.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:46.080
Amazing.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.540
Don't break formation!
Unit two, we need backup!

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.170
Are you really a rich kid?

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:52.210
Shut up!

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.300
We're doing this in one shot!

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.430
If they take that fortress,

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:07.230
this war will be over soon.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.150
I see.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:13.440
But as long as Prince Rudo is here,
your future looks bleak...

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.110
So, please run away.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:20.450
When this war ends,
go somewhere far away with Mr. Leobolt!

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.910
I have an idea.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:29.250
It's a pillow!

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:31.630
A soft pillow!

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:36.630
That kid is pretty curious.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.550
He really admires you.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.800
I don't do any research anymore.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:45.850
Weren't you hired by the Capital Army?

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:48.270
I'm not in the military.

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:52.100
The Capital Army just stole my research.

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:54.440
They stole everything.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:58.070
Then the airship is still in the hands
of the Army?

00:10:58.900 --> 00:10:59.900
Anyway,

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:04.740
why is someone like you here
instead of in the Capital?

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:07.370
What are you doing traveling around

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:09.870
with those kids?

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:15.290
I'm also someone who doesn't agree
with what the Capital Army is doing.

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:17.000
I just...

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:19.970
found a ray of hope.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:23.260
<i>I wonder what this box is.</i>

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:28.100
It has five dials.
I wonder if it's a code.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.520
Try entering each word in one by one!

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.350
Don't be ridiculous!

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:36.440
A quick calculation shows that there
are over 300 million combinations!

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:38.650
Then it's impossible!

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:41.780
There must be a hint somewhere.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.120
Is it the name of a place or a person?

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:45.990
Or an object?

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:50.580
We're looking for someone named Finis.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:51.910
Do you know her?

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.460
I don't know her.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:59.670
-What if--?
-Did you figure it out?

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.970
Finis.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:04.680
It opened!

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.760
You did it! Al, you're a genius!

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:10.600
I feel like I've seen these
somewhere before.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.070
They're the same.

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:22.650
-What in the world are they?
-It's an Echo Device.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.580
Sorry! I didn't mean to--

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.450
It hasn't been charged yet.
You barely escaped alive.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:35.790
That's ammunition for a Symphony Killer.

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:39.880
It's a tool for killing people in wars.

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:42.840
Why is something like this here?

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:46.550
Because I made it.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:54.730
So, you were helping the war, too.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:58.310
That might have been the result
in the end.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.190
"The result"?

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:04.360
Let me tell you about Finis.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.950
She was able to create

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:12.080
all kinds of miracles
with the power of her songs.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.920
The miracles were based on earth,
wind, water, and fire,

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:21.670
which are the Four Great Elements
from which the world is made of.

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:27.260
Everything in this world is made up
of the Four Great Elements.

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.180
The Four Great Elements.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.970
It's the same as the spirits.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:33.640
Spirits, huh?

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:36.230
That's a good way to put it.

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:40.400
<i>To contribute to the future</i>
<i>of the Capital,</i>

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:43.690
<i>I scientifically analyzed the power</i>
<i>of songs</i>

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:47.030
<i>and conducted research to see</i>
<i>if we could use it for anything.</i>

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:51.580
<i>And then I finally invented</i>
<i>the Echo Device.</i>

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.660
<i>What is that?</i>

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:57.540
It preserves the power of songs.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.840
Was that the Song of Fire?

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:14.100
Songs are made of sounds that are
transmitted through the air. Waves.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:18.690
The songs can be made to echo infinitely
within a device made

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:21.270
from a special material
and preserved semi-permanently.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:25.610
When the songs are played back,
the power of the songs materializes.

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:28.400
There was a song inside that box?

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:31.740
Theoretically,
we can even preserve the past.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:32.830
The past?

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:36.160
Songs and sounds from the past
can drift around as waves

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:41.210
without attenuation
within this special environment.

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.000
If they can be replayed,

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:46.960
then the situation
at that time will unfold.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.800
Don't worry about her.

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:52.050
Well, in any case,

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.350
with the Echo Device,
we can create miracles

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:57.770
without placing a burden on the singer.

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:02.350
So, then I designed a machine
to amplify the power

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:05.480
that was preserved within the Echo Device
to its maximum strength.

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:07.320
Do you mean--?

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:12.820
The weapon you saw that plays songs.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:16.450
That thing called the Symphony Killer.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:20.250
<i>The Capital Army said</i>
<i>they were going to use Finis's songs</i>

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.960
<i>and my invention as weapons of war.</i>

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:26.630
<i>The objects I had designed</i>
<i>to bring happiness to people</i>

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.710
<i>were going to be used to kill people.</i>

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:31.680
<i>I was against it.</i>

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:35.430
<i>But the Capital Army wouldn't listen</i>
<i>to me.</i>

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:39.980
As a result, they confiscated
my inventions and the Echo Device.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:43.230
And they used me and threw me away.

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.820
I gave up on everything.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:48.780
No way.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:51.610
How could you give up on your dream?

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.570
Why don't you make another invention?

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.120
They took everything away from me!

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:03.540
They attacked this place
with the Song of Water many times.

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:07.090
The research facility
I spent my entire life building

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:08.340
was sunk underwater!

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:10.630
Do you mean--?

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:21.770
<i>I had many researchers,</i>
<i>but they're all dead now!</i>

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:23.640
<i>Can you even understand?</i>

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:25.850
<i>The days and years it took</i>

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:29.650
<i>to bury all the corpses</i>
<i>of my dear researchers!</i>

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:31.990
There's no way you could understand!

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:38.660
If you defy the Capital Army,
you'll lose whatever's important to you.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:42.870
I lost something, too.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:45.370
Rin.

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:50.420
That's why I sing.
I don't want to lose anything anymore.

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:54.760
I made a promise to someone important.
That's why I sing.

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:07.480
<i>Terra</i>

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:10.480
<i>Mater</i>

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:13.650
<i>Terra</i>

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:16.910
<i>Mater</i>

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:23.200
<i>Embraced by the earth</i>

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:29.540
<i>Feel your heart throb</i>

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:36.220
<i>Embraced by the earth</i>

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:43.560
<i>Life awakens</i>

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:48.690
It's a miracle.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.480
Rin, you're...

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.530
Thank you!

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:09.670
The Capital Army is victorious!

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:13.590
I can't believe we really conquered them.

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:27.640
To our leader!

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:29.350
To our leader!

00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:35.030
To our leader! To our leader!

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:37.110
To our leader!

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:38.030
Henry!

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:40.280
To our leader!

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.160
To our leader!

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:46.250
-To our leader!
<i>-An airship!</i>

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:49.710
I've never seen one before!

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:51.670
Me neither!

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:55.800
I wonder what the Capital Army
is trying to do.

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:57.550
I don't know.

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:02.180
However, the Symphony Killer
and the airship were both headed

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:04.260
in the direction of Ash City.

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.640
Ash City?

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:08.230
That's in the frontline region
on the border.

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:10.730
Finis is probably there, too.

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:15.230
The price she pays for the power of songs
is a shorter life.

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:18.530
It looks like you're an exception.

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:24.370
The Capital Army is abusing Finis.
She doesn't have a lot of time left.

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:26.030
Then we have to hurry!

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:28.910
We're going to help Finis.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.630
Thanks for everything, genius old man.

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:38.800
Oh, hey, kid.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:40.970
-Your name's Al, right?
-Yes?

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.050
Stay with me.

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:48.390
I've got something I can use to repay you
for your kindness.

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:53.350
I want this kid to help me
while I complete it.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:58.570
I've never heard of anyone being
scouted directly by Dr. Weissen before!

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:00.110
That's amazing!

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:01.530
Al?

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:05.160
I'm deeply honored.

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:07.490
But I'm sorry.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.620
I have to stay with Rin.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:16.250
I'm not a member of her Orchestra,
and I can't use the power of songs.

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:19.960
I make a bunch of weird inventions,
and I'm useless.

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:21.550
I know that.

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:26.600
But I still promised to protect Rin.

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:28.510
You did it, Al.

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:32.600
Being hired by the genius old man

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:36.690
brings you closer to leaving your name
in the history of the Capital!

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:40.280
I'll be fine.

00:20:40.730 --> 00:20:43.900
Everyone else is still here.
And I'm sure Mr. Leobolt will help us.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.660
-But...
-And Mel, too.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:49.580
I'm sure Mel supports your dream, too.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:56.000
Without you,
we wouldn't have made it this far.

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.720
Are you okay, Rin?

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:11.970
Al is part of my family.
We've always been together.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:14.600
He's the only family I have.

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:19.520
So, that's why even if we're apart,
I'm sure--

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:21.320
She's a country girl!

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:25.030
She's a pig and she's an idiot!

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:27.660
But...

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:31.120
please take good care of Rin!

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:39.540
Idiot.

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:41.460
You're acting like her parent!

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:43.050
A doting parent.

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:54.470
You'll see her again soon.

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:56.100
You're a man. Don't cry.

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:57.440
Yes.

00:21:59.230 --> 00:22:00.860
What's that piece of paper?

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:08.570
How are the preparations
for the Court Orchestra?

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:11.160
Sir. The preparations are complete.

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:16.160
When this song echoes
throughout the Star Song Festival,

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:18.040
everything will begin!
